  "scrub": [
    "Temp roots are replaced by name inside every string: <STATE_DIR>, <WORKSPACE_ROOT>, <WORKTREE_ROOT>, <HOME> (the throwaway HOME); the tether checkout becomes <TETHER_REPO> and the operator's real home <OPERATOR_HOME>; any other os.tmpdir() path becomes <TMP>; a temp dir's basename inside text becomes tether-parity-<kind>-XXXXXX.",
    "The server's loopback origin 127.0.0.1:<port> becomes 127.0.0.1:<PORT>; a numeric field named `port` inside a worktree service keeps its type but is set to 0.",
    "Epoch-millisecond numbers (1.5e12..2.5e12) become 1767225600000 and epoch-second numbers under a key ending in At/at/Time become 1767225600 (types are preserved); ISO-8601 timestamps inside strings become 2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z.",
    "Duration-like numbers (keys ending in Ms / ms / Seconds, or named elapsed/duration/latency/uptime/pid) become 0; a parenthesized duration inside text, e.g. `(16 ms)`, becomes `(0 ms)`.",
    "Server-minted ids are replaced by stable ordinals in first-seen order, everywhere they occur (including inside larger strings): UUIDs -> 00000000-0000-4000-8000-<12-digit ordinal>; Tether session ids -> sess-<n>; schedule ids -> sched-<n>; other minted base64url ids under an `id`/`…Id` key (history ids, …) -> id-<n>; 40-hex git shas -> <sha-n>; worktree project hashes -> <project-hash-n>.",
    "Ordering: scenario frames are in arrival order except that, between two client frames, server frames are grouped per socket (primary first) and session rows are coalesced to the last row per session, placed after that socket's other frames. Ambient frames (log records, unsolicited catalog/registry pushes, metrics-only or repeated session rows) are split out — see manifest.ambient and canonicalOrder. Every client frame is sent only after 150 ms of wire silence, and each scenario ends after a full 2.5 s metrics-sweep period.",
    "Not scrubbed: host-dependent values (CLI detection/versions in server-settings `detected`/`discovered`) — stable across re-runs on one host, but they differ between hosts."
  ]
}
